 "notes": "Right page (p.113) holds the ledger grid; left page (p.112) holds the single printed annotation. Year is 1938 throughout (data spans OCT.25 to DEC.8, though dated rows after 28 are blank). Grid dates present but blank: 26, 28, SAT.29, 31, 2, 4, SAT.5, 14, 15, 16, 17, SAT.19, 21, 22, 23, 25, 29, 30, DEC.1, 2, SAT.3, 5, 6, 7, 8 (no Sunday rows; row 8 is skipped in the Nov date column between 7 and 9). Only rows with handwritten entries are transcribed. All entries fall in Upward Trend (black ink) for OCT.25 through SAT.12, then Natural Reaction (blue pencil) for the 18/SAT.26/28 reaction leg. Every row where all three instruments are present satisfies KP = US + BS. Row 18 US eighths (1/8) vs BS eighths (7/8) were disambiguated by the KP=137 checksum. SAT.12 pivotal top carries red single underlines under all three figures; row 28 pivotal low carries dark (black/blue) single underlines under all three, verified as heavier and number-width, separate from the full-width red printed grid rule beneath them.",
